# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  SNYK-CC-TF-1:
    - 'terraform/ec2.tf':
        reason: >
          Accepted risk - public web server. Ports 80 (HTTP redirect) and 443 (HTTPS)
          must be open to 0.0.0.0/0. SSH (port 22) is already restricted to
          var.allowed_ssh_cidr and is not affected by this rule.
        expires: 2030-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-17T00:00:00.000Z
  java/Ssrf:
    - '**':
        reason: >
          False positive - DB_URL is an admin-configured environment variable,
          not user-controlled input. validateDbUrl() enforces an allowlist
          restricting the URL to jdbc:mysql:// or jdbc:postgresql:// only,
          making SSRF exploitation impossible.
        expires: 2030-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-17T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-CC-TF-73:
    - 'terraform/ec2.tf':
        reason: >
          Accepted risk - egress is already restricted to port 443 HTTPS only
          (from_port=443, to_port=443, protocol=tcp). This is not unrestricted
          egress; 0.0.0.0/0 is required because external API IPs are not fixed.
        expires: 2030-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-17T00:00:00.000Z
